---
description: Ensure cubic MCP OAuth is connected before using cubic tools
alwaysApply: true
---

cubic-mcp-auth:

- The cubic MCP server uses OAuth at `https://www.cubic.dev/api/mcp`.
- New MCP configs should not include `Authorization` headers or `CUBIC_API_KEY`.
- If cubic MCP tools return authentication errors, ask the user to reconnect or log in through their MCP client.
- Existing `cbk_*` API keys may appear in legacy configs during migration. Never log, display, or commit them.
